"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-2a\" transform=\"translate(59.796875 0)\"/></g></g></g><g id=\"patch_3\"><path d=\"M 58.873736 139.04 L 148.733476 139.04 L 148.733476 119.146406 L 58.873736 119.146406 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6765345a06)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_4\"><path d=\"M 171.198411 139.04 L 261.058151 139.04 L 261.058151 51.448802 L 171.198411 51.448802 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6765345a06)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 283.523086 139.04 L 373.382827 139.04 L 373.382827 17.6 L 283.523086 17.6 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6765345a06)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 43.148281 139.04 L 43.148281 11.528 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_7\"><path d=\"M 43.148281 139.04 L 389.108281 139.04 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(95.515481 116.946406) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(207.840156 49.248802) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" d=\"M 3187 4467 L 3187 3994 L 1229 3994 L 1101 2291 L 1146 2291 Q 1254 2445 1376 2553 Q 1498 2662 1664 2723 Q 1830 2784 2061 2784 Q 2445 2784 2745 2617 Q 3046 2451 3219 2144 Q 3392 1837 3392 1402 Q 3392 966 3213 633 Q 3034 301 2698 112 Q 2362 -77 1888 -77 Q 1517 -77 1254 35 Q 992 147 809 320 Q 627 493 493 685 L 896 992 Q 1069 730 1277 566 Q 1485 403 1888 403 Q 2342 403 2582 646 Q 2822 890 2822 1331 L 2822 1395 Q 2822 1837 2582 2080 Q 2342 2323 1888 2323 Q 1581 2323 1405 2211 Q 1229 2099 1088 1946 L 634 2010 L 794 4467 L 3187 4467 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(320.164832 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\" d=\"M 1696 0 L 1120 0 L 2829 4006 L 922 4006 L 922 3174 L 442 3174 L 442 4467 L 3373 4467 L 3373 3994 L 1696 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p6765345a06\"><rect x=\"43.148281\" y=\"11.528\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Operating profit by year ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Profit = (members × $95 × 12 + $0.45M) × 95% − $0.95M.</p> <ul><li>Year 1: 600 members → <b>$0.13M</b></li><li>Year 2: 1,000 members → <b>$0.56M</b></li><li>Year 3: 1,200 members → <b>$0.78M</b></li></ul> <p>Cumulative after three years: $1.46M of the $2.2M. At year-three profit, the remaining $0.74M takes another 0.9 years: payback ≈ <b>3.9 years</b>, inside the five-year hurdle.</p>"},{"q":"Members climb 2.2 times a week; 40% of visits are in the weekday 6-9pm peak (15 hours a week); a session lasts 2 hours. How many people are in the gym at peak with 1,200 members? (Assume day-pass visitors climb mostly at weekends and off-peak, so ignore them for the evening peak.)","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Peak arrivals per hour: 1,200 × 2.2 × 40% ÷ 15 = 70.4.</p> <p>Each stays 2 hours, so about <b>141 people</b> are climbing at once, against a safe limit of 120.</p> <p>Maximum members before peak overcrowding: 1,200 × 120 ÷ 141 ≈ <b>1,023</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the plan's year-three membership doesn't physically fit. Unless peak demand is shifted, membership caps at about 1,023.</p>","note":"This is the crux of the case. Strong candidates spot the capacity question before being asked."},{"q":"What does the cap do to the investment case?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>At about 1,023 members, steady-state profit is $0.59M instead of $0.78M. Payback stretches: after year two the remaining $1.51M takes 2.6 more years: about <b>4.6 years</b>, still inside five, but with little margin.</p> <p><b>Fixes:</b> off-peak memberships at a lower price (students, shift workers, parents), corporate memberships used at lunchtime, timed booking at peak, and a higher peak-access price.</p>"},{"q":"What would you recommend to the investors?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Go ahead, but redesign the membership model before opening: an off-peak tier priced ~30% lower, a peak tier priced higher, and pre-sold corporate memberships for daytime use. Track peak occupancy from day one.</p>"}],"reco":"Go ahead, with a different membership model. On the plan's numbers the gym pays back in about 3.9 years, but at 1,200 members about 141 people would be climbing at peak against a safe limit of 120, so membership effectively caps at about 1,023 and payback stretches to about 4.6 years. I recommend launching with peak and off-peak tiers and pre-selling daytime corporate memberships to grow beyond the cap. Risk: if off-peak demand is weak, payback lands close to the hurdle. Next step: survey local climbers on when they would visit and at what price.","great":["Models the ramp-up instead of using steady state from day one","Checks physical capacity at peak","Converts the capacity limit into a membership cap","Fixes the problem with pricing tiers, not just 'more marketing'"],"id":34,"slug":"orbit-climbing"}